code: K0040
title: Function Missing Result Type
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, function, return-type, type-annotation]
description: "Function declaration is missing a ': ReturnType' annotation"
---

Function declarations require an explicit `: ReturnType` annotation between the parameter list `(...)` and `=>`.

## Example

This error occurs when `=>` immediately follows the parameter list without a `: Type` return annotation:

```kura
fn add(a: Int, b: Int) => a + b

fn greeting() => #text("Hello")
```

## Solution

Add `: Type` after the parameter list to specify the function's return type:

```kura
fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int => a + b

fn greeting(): Element => #text("Hello")
```
